From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:49:28 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] psDooM: processes as monsters, through libpsd

psDooM's hooks on Chocolate Doom, calling the shared glue in
engines/common/psdoom (psdoom-plus tree) and libpsd. Generated with
tools/apply-doom-hooks.py:

- p_mobj.h, r_defs.h: pid, label and flags on things and vissprites
- d_main.c: psdoom1/2.wad after the IWAD (unless -nopslev); open libpsd
- p_setup.c, p_tick.c: forget/spawn per level, poll every tic
- p_inter.c: only players hurt pid monsters (-nopssafety); damage
  renices, death kills, a vanished process drops nothing
- p_mobj.c: removal bookkeeping; -respawnitems
- p_saveg.c: pid monsters aren't saved; resync after loading
- g_game.c: -nomonsters. persists
- r_things.c: the floating 'pid / name' label
- m_menu.c: M_WriteText and M_StartMessage are callable by the glue
---
 src/doom/d_main.c   |  3 +++
 src/doom/g_game.c   |  4 ++++
 src/doom/m_menu.c   |  4 ++--
 src/doom/p_inter.c  | 12 ++++++++++++
 src/doom/p_mobj.c   |  4 +++-
 src/doom/p_mobj.h   |  7 +++++++
 src/doom/p_saveg.c  |  4 ++++
 src/doom/p_setup.c  |  4 ++++
 src/doom/p_tick.c   |  2 ++
 src/doom/r_defs.h   |  5 +++++
 src/doom/r_things.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 11 files changed, 62 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

